  m_Name: LorePart2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LoreData
  title: REPORT N.20012002
  loreText: "Year 2001. Using the Volot device, the first expedition into the first
    phase of the subspace was carried out. Communication between the exploration
    team and the engineers remained stable. Eventually, the following was discovered:
    the robots that had previously assisted in Mirium mining had become hostile and
    began attacking the exploration team. All of their actions\u2014attacks and retreats
    alike\u2014were chaotic and uncoordinated. During the second expedition, an armed
    unit was sent to accompany the exploration team. However, things turned out far
    worse than the scientists had expected. This time, the robots\u2019 movements
    were no longer chaotic\u2014they knew exactly what they were doing, using various
    tactics as if they were being controlled. This provided the scientists with a
    crucial insight: Mirium is intelligent and capable of adaptation. After several
    successful expeditions, the military decided to use Mirium in the production
    of weapons for protecting exploration teams. As expected, Mirium replicated these
    weapons, and the fight against robots infected with Mirium became significantly
    more difficult. These machines were designated as the \u201CLost Ones.\u201D\n\n
    Year 2002. A new research complex, \u201CBabylon,\u201D established to deal with
    the Mirium catastrophe in the Mirny-13 exclusion zone, announced the existence
    of the second and third phases of the subspace. In each of these phases, visibility
    gradually decreases due to dense fog. The Lost Ones are present in all phases,
    and with each deeper level they become more intelligent. They also become more
    aggressive, and their physical capabilities increase every time an exploration
    unit advances to a new phase. However, no one in the facility could have imagined
    that this so-called \u201Crabbit hole\u201D might be even deeper... One of the
    exploration teams reported that after collecting a sufficient amount of Mirium
    in the third phase of the subspace, the entire group was transported to the fourth
    phase. At first glance, this phase was almost identical to the others, with one
    crucial difference\u2014a massive entity awaited there, surpassing all other
    Lost Ones in both size and physical power. The exploration team also noticed
    that this entity was guarding a strange levitating object similar to the allied
    Volot. It was surrounded by two massive black-violet pillars capable of summoning
    Lost Ones from other parts of the subspace to assist the monster. Scientists
    assumed it was a modified version of Volot, created either by Mirium itself or
    by an unknown entity within the subspace. The entity from the fourth phase was
    named the \u201CGuardian,\u201D and the Mirium-altered device was designated
    the \u201CDark Tower.\u201D"
